{
  "name": "GFS 2m temperature (Climate Reanalyzer style)",
  "units": "degC",
  "source": "Colour values sampled from a Climate Reanalyzer GFS 2m temperature colourbar (Climate Change Institute, University of Maine). Credit the data source if you reproduce their imagery; the ramp itself is a functional lookup table.",
  "domain": {
    "min": -60,
    "max": 50,
    "band_width": 1,
    "band_count": 110
  },
  "overflow": {
    "below_min": "#FFFFFF",
    "above_max": "#8B8B8B"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Canonical form is the discrete 110-band table: band i covers [lower, upper).",
    "There is a deliberate hard discontinuity at 0 C (cyan -> green) marking the freezing line. Do not smooth across it.",
    "The continuous knot list is a convenience for smooth shading. It reproduces the band table to within ~4/255 per channel except below -55 C, where the source ramp is coarsely stepped and error reaches ~19/255 in pale lavender.",
    "This is a rainbow-family scale: not colourblind-safe and it creates apparent edges at hue transitions. That is accepted here because meteorology audiences read this convention fluently."
  ],
